From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 01:43:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] services: ANSI RPC entry points, EnumServiceGroup,
 ControlServiceEx, QueryServiceConfigEx, preferred node, lock status (3214)

CORE review. The interface's ANSI functions (OpenSCManagerA, OpenServiceA, CreateService[WOW64]A,
ChangeServiceConfig[2]A, QueryServiceConfig[2]A, StartServiceA, EnumServicesStatus[Ex]A,
EnumDependentServicesA, Get*NameA, QueryServiceLockStatusA) convert and run the wide ones;
REnumServiceGroupW, RControlServiceEx[AW], RQueryServiceConfigEx (trigger information),
RQueryServiceStatus, RQueryServiceLockStatus[W], RNotifyBootConfigStatus and
SERVICE_CONFIG_PREFERRED_NODE (services.exe, svcctl.idl, sechost) are implemented; the opnums
MS-SCMR marks "reserved for local use" stay unserved.  ChangeServiceConfig with a NULL
dependencies argument no longer removes the existing dependencies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZFS4SPPzeH5d2c1MuzqCS

